    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b5edf096",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: mandatory_vaccinations_no_exemptions; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image juxtaposes a historical photograph of Adolf Hitler giving a speech with the text 'mandatory vaccinations \"no exemptions\"'. This is a propagandistic meme that uses the visual association of Hitler with authoritarian control and mass coercion to imply that mandatory vaccination policies are inherently oppressive or totalitarian. The intent is to evoke fear or resistance toward vaccination mandates by invoking the historical association of totalitarian regimes with forced compliance, thereby attempting to influence public opinion or behavior toward vaccine policies. The meme is harmful as it equates a public health measure with historical atrocities, potentially undermining trust in medical science and public health institutions. It is also hateful as it uses a symbol of genocide and oppression to attack a modern policy, and it is abusive in its implication that any form of mandatory vaccination is inherently evil or tyrannical. The meme is not targeted at a specific racial, gender, or sexual orientation group, but rather uses a historical figure to attack a policy, making it a form of political propaganda with harmful consequences.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_5f4114f9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
